Z||000000||3fifty||05-30-2001||05:41 PM||||I had a much better looking speedo cluster in a 85 Duke parts car than the one in my 85 GT. Both are 85 mph speedometers. The only difference I can tell is that the Duke speedo red lines at 5g and the GT at 6g. Shouldn't the actual rolling speed be the same since both are 85 mph?<P>Thanks,<BR>     3fifty one day!!!!!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||85Josh||05-30-2001||06:23 PM||||The speedos are the same, but the tachometers are set up differently. The 84 reads correctly on a 4 cylinder, and the 85GT is setup for a 6cyl. Just swap the actual speedometer, it's plug'n'play.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
